1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,560
Keep running along, watch as we pass by,
as we raise our flag, up high in the sky.

2
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:13,570
Alright,

3
00:00:13,653 --> 00:00:18,011
here we go now, sailing through the
endless ocean, facing all that comes by.

4
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:23,960
Let's look for our treasure, nobody has
ever got to witness with their own eyes.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,617
All we have to do is keep believing in our
dreams, And let our heart lead the way!

6
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:33,820
Then once we got all the
others left is to go,

7
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:39,217
When we face the dark and stormy weather?

8
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,177
Keep the pace, we'll
link our hearts together!

9
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:45,720
Then I'm sure we'll make it through!

10
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:47,777
No matter what!

11
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:51,457
Keep running along, keep running along!

12
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:54,397
Start raising our flag as we journey on!

13
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:59,537
Though our chances are close to
none, We won't back down from anyone!

14
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:03,437
Let's start off the chase,
let's start off the chase!

15
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:06,397
Toward our own dreams,
while keeping the pace!

16
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:08,737
With a compass pointing to our goal!

17
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:13,460
We won't stop till we've
gone around the world!

18
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,900
Start me up!

19
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:21,417
Keep running along, keep running along!

20
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:24,357
And we'll never stop,
till we're at the top!

21
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:26,737
There's no way that we'll ever quit!

22
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:29,380
Won't keep heading for tomorrow!

23
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,957
Let's start up the chase!

24
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:33,457
Let's start up the chase!

25
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:34,997
I see through your eyes!

26
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:36,397
What we'll have to face!

27
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:39,017
All the memories will stay in our hearts!

28
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:41,297
We'll never let them go!

29
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:43,380
Brand new world!

30
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:45,880
Let's start me up!

31
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,140
Hey, look!

32
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:13,321
They're opening!

33
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:15,357
The Gates of Justice are really opening!

34
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:16,270
You're right!

35
00:02:16,353 --> 00:02:19,885
In all my years here, this is the
first time it's ever happened!

36
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:24,107
I've never even heard
of it happening before!

37
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,757
We must be letting the
battleships from the headquarters

38
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:30,080
through the Buster Call
is about to let loose

39
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,857
Crap I don't like this.

40
00:02:36,940 --> 00:02:41,175
Granny Kokoro said the Gates of Justice
never open all the way like that

41
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:44,317
This Buster Call thing
must be really bad Even

42
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,497
the Marines are in a
panic to get out of here.

43
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:49,517
The Straw Hats picked a fight
with the whole world They

44
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:52,776
might really burn down the
whole island to get at them

45
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:55,497
Bring it in there, bro!

46
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:56,440
Don't die!

47
00:02:57,060 --> 00:02:57,890
Yeah!

48
00:02:58,460 --> 00:03:00,720
You too, Straw Hat! Kill me!

49
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,840
Robin will be fine.

50
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:20,258
I know Franky can take care of her.

51
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:22,817
I was careless.

52
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:26,000
Yes, this new power of
his took me by surprise.

53
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:29,960
Whatever you're doing seems
to be taking its toll.

54
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:33,022
In shame, the fight was
just getting interesting.

55
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:39,660
I don't care what happens.

56
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:42,160
As long as I can beat you.

57
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,000
I see.

58
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:48,300
How stubborn.

59
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:51,920
Almost there!

60
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:55,076
Don't you dare leave yet, Nico Robin!

61
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,720
Guards, on to the bridge!

62
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:00,740
Yes, sir!

63
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:10,340
All right, men. Ready? Good!

64
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:13,541
Because Chief Spondheim
is on his way as we speak.

65
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:16,517
He's delivering an
especially heinous criminal

66
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:18,277
across the bridge from the Tower of Law.

67
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,980
This doesn't happen often,

68
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,117
so I want all marines
from the escort ships

69
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:24,897
and all guards from the
gate here in top form!

70
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:27,509
Give them the best
dance salute you've got!

71
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:39,400
Would you look at that!

72
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:41,720
All lined up and ready to sail!

73
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,880
Not a thing left to stop me!

74
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,477
Oh, I almost forgot.

75
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:54,080
There's a surprise waiting
for your little friends.

76
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:55,490
You see,

77
00:04:55,573 --> 00:04:56,637
before we cross the bridge,

78
00:04:56,720 --> 00:05:00,237
I set up a landmine at the top
of those stairs right over there.

79
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:03,977
So in the unlikely event that someone
actually does come to save you,

80
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:06,900
they and the stairs will both go BOOM!

81
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:10,288
Quite the elegant
solution, don't you think?

82
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:12,760
Well, I'm excited at least.

83
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:16,037
Though I suppose neither of us
should get our hopes up too much,

84
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:20,061
Seeing as how no one will be coming
to help you in the first place!

85
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:27,157
I won't go through that gate.

86
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,240
What?

87
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:41,760
I still believe they'll come to
save me They're not coming, okay?

88
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,510
Gee, shut up!

89
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:47,797
They'll be burned to a crisp Just like
everything else in the Buster Calls path.

90
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:48,710
You got that?

91
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:51,320
Rather convenient, really.

92
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:55,037
Every humiliation I've suffered,
including them shooting down our flag,

93
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,520
will be erased as well.

94
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:03,960
Just like before, 20 years ago, when
that marine giant attacked us in Ohala.

95
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,960
Now it's time to walk.

96
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:09,800
That means on your own two feet, damn it.

97
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:11,750
Saul.

98
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,000
Hurry up!

99
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:18,160
Are you okay, chief?

100
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:19,190
Do you need help?

101
00:06:19,273 --> 00:06:20,677
No, I don't need any help.

102
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:22,407
Dammit, I'm a friggin' hero!

103
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:27,234
If you thought I didn't know anything
about that, then you're dead wrong.

104
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:31,980
Your old friend Jaguar de Sol was a
vice-admiral before he betrayed us.

105
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:34,600
Your mother, Olvia, was an archaeologist.

106
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:37,700
And I know about your
hometown of Ohara as well.

107
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:40,640
Quite the tragic tale, isn't it?

108
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:43,280
And why do I know all this?

109
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,972
Well, it's quite simple.

110
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:47,957
Because the man who
commanded the raid on Ohara,

111
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:52,687
uncovered their crimes, then blew the
island to smithereens with a Buster Call?

112
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:55,600
was the chief of CP9 who preceded me!

113
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:59,440
Otherwise known as my father, Spandine!

114
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:10,760
Well, scholars of Ohara, I'm afraid your
death sentence has already been decided.

115
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,540
Kill him!

116
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:31,500
You left us no choice.

117
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:36,420
Ohara knows too much.

118
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:38,520
I invoke the Buster Call.

119
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,700
And that's a wrap.

120
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,640
Hurry, take her and go, Saul

121
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:57,200
Are you sure? Yeah.

122
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:01,437
Stop it, I want to stay with you, mommy!

123
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:07,340
I was happy to hear
you call me back again.

124
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:09,437
Thank you.

125
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,037
From now on.

126
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,740
For my sake as well.

127
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,960
You must live, Robin!

128
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:27,220
At the time, they thought that everyone
in Ohara had been nicely eliminated.

129
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:32,466
But they found out later that one little
brat had slipped through their fingers.

130
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:35,257
So, how was it?

131
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:38,057
Running from one money-grubbing
adult to the next,

132
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:40,787
hoping you weren't either
killed or sold out.

133
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:46,177
Not a single person you
could trust no matter where

134
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:49,257
you went nowhere to lay your
little head down in peace

135
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:53,517
nothing to eat what a vile
and wretched existence

136
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:56,780
you've had why it's too
appalling to even think about

137
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:04,820
sad enough to make you cry huh 20 years
ago my old man put that bounty on your

138
00:09:09,620 --> 00:09:11,897
little hand, all for world peace.

139
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:13,917
Show some gratitude, will you?

140
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,420
Now we finally have our happy ending.

141
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:21,132
The son completes the father's crusade
against the devils of Ohara, and the

142
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:24,517
wrongs of 20 years ago have
been made right at last.

143
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:26,760
Ohara is dead!

144
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,260
Don't cry Robin, but be proud.

145
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:34,937
Your mama's a wonderful woman.

146
00:09:35,020 --> 00:09:36,900
Ohara's a wonderful place.

147
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:38,837
You gotta remember that.

148
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:40,979
It's up to you to pass it on, okay.

149
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,677
Ohara was so brave.

150
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,878
They fought against the whole world.

151
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:54,740
Ohara won't die as long as I live. Yeah?

152
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:57,760
And how long is that going to be? Huh?

153
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,030
Whoa!

154
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:09,220
The egg went off!

155
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:16,960
Cutty Flam!

156
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:18,920
What is he doing here?

157
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:20,600
Well, no harm done.

158
00:10:20,980 --> 00:10:23,060
He fell for the landmine. Idiot!

159
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:24,220
Serves you right!

160
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:32,460
He came to rescue me still that was close
it's a good thing i had my backup plan.

161
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:38,297
Come on let's go i'm so angry i can't

162
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:41,117
even speak all right marine set sail.

163
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:45,357
We're getting out of here
now understood sir everyone

164
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:49,980
move yes sir i can't hold
back the tears anymore?

165
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:58,857
Watch carefully men because you're about
to witness the first step of a hero!

166
00:10:58,940 --> 00:11:01,380
that is destined to go down in history!

167
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:18,360
Are you okay, Chief? What happened?

168
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:20,840
He was hit! We're under attack!

169
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:22,677
There's no one on the bridge but us!

170
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:23,590
No!

171
00:11:23,673 --> 00:11:24,957
They must be hiding somewhere!

172
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:26,511
Everyone start searching!

173
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:27,770
But where?

174
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:29,350
Huh?

175
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,610
Hey!

176
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:39,837
What's wrong with you?

177
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:40,750
Fight back!

178
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:42,260
Don't just stand there!

179
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:45,836
Betrayed, sir, but we don't
know where the enemy's at!

180
00:11:48,620 --> 00:11:49,450
There!

181
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:10,177
he's standing on top of the
tower of law what's he doing

182
00:12:10,260 --> 00:12:13,980
up there it's so far away
How the hell's he hitting us?

183
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:22,620
Is he using a slingshot?

184
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:24,440
This guy's a monster.

185
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:27,597
The wind runs like crazy, and
he's all the way over there,

186
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:30,209
but he's still hitting
his mark every time.

187
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,320
Thank you, Long Nose.

188
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:34,560
Bam, eat that.

189
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:36,620
Our sniper is number one.

190
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:40,140
Serves you right, bastards.

191
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:41,820
Come on, Robin, run!

192
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:45,320
I can do without the singing, I think.

193
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,270
Team!

194
00:12:54,820 --> 00:12:55,820
Damn it!

195
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,529
What are you idiots doing?

196
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:59,220
Shoot that guy already!

197
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:00,570
We're trying,

198
00:13:00,653 --> 00:13:05,117
sir, but he's too far away for our bullets
to reach, let alone to actually hit him.

199
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:08,318
I hate to say it, but he's
got us totally outclassed!

200
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:10,140
Nico Robin is getting away!

201
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:11,597
Then stop her!

202
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:13,720
Shoot her down, sir.

203
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:16,960
Shoot her just dead
enough to keep her alive

204
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,680
Who the hell is that?

205
00:14:12,820 --> 00:14:13,650
Franky...

206
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:17,977
Bullets are no problem
when you're made of iron.

207
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:21,020
But that landmine wasn't
very nice, Spanda.

208
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:23,390
Franky!

209
00:14:23,473 --> 00:14:24,420
Come in, Franky!

210
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:25,442
Do you read me?

211
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:27,580
This is Sniper King! Huh?

212
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:30,137
Yeah, I can read you
loud and clear, but...

213
00:14:30,220 --> 00:14:31,050
How?

214
00:14:31,133 --> 00:14:32,300
I got the snail from Nami.

215
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:34,076
Anyway, turn around.

216
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:37,435
There should be a red bundle
on the ground next to you.

217
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:38,650
Red bundle?

218
00:14:38,733 --> 00:14:40,160
Oh, I see it. Good.

219
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:41,960
It has two keys inside.

220
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:45,749
Together with the ones you have,
that should be all of them.

221
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,660
How did they get the keys?

222
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:51,360
And my mission is complete.

223
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:53,560
Nice work.

224
00:14:54,780 --> 00:14:56,860
All right, then. Let's go.

225
00:14:57,060 --> 00:15:02,640
Number one, number three,
number four, number five.

226
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:05,680
We got it!

227
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:11,620
No way!

228
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:13,705
This can't be happening to me!

229
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,220
Oh, hold on.

230
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:18,680
We're not in the clear yet. But wait!

231
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:19,820
That means...

232
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:22,980
They really did it?

233
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:26,760
A bunch of useless pirates
beat every last member of CP9?

234
00:15:34,660 --> 00:15:36,280
No, that can't be right.

235
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:38,717
They must have just stolen
the keys and run away!

236
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:40,180
Hey, bunch of cheaters!

237
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:42,460
Okay, we got it!

238
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:43,980
Hey, you hear me?

239
00:15:44,340 --> 00:15:47,820
We got the handcuffs off
Robin, no problem! Yes!

240
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:49,800
Thank you, Longhouse.

241
00:15:50,020 --> 00:15:51,138
That was wonderful.

242
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:53,177
It was the least I could do.

243
00:15:53,260 --> 00:15:57,557
The true heroes are those who fought
to retrieve those keys from the enemy.

244
00:15:57,640 --> 00:16:00,317
The Straw Hats will be
proud to have you back.

245
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:04,929
Hold your head up high and meet them
with a smile when all of this has ended.

246
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:06,710
Right.

247
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:11,040
No, c 'est fleur.

248
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:13,600
What the?

249
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:15,190
Slap.

250
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:26,940
I've been waiting a long time to do this.

251
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:37,197
Are you okay, chief?

252
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:39,140
All right, let's move.

253
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:40,797
Get your asses over here.

254
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:42,597
I'll get everything ready for you.

255
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:44,240
We're gonna bail. Roger!

256
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:48,200
Get down here already, Sniper King.

257
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:51,777
The prisoners escaped from the
same prism stone handcuffs.

258
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:53,620
Regroup and recapture her!

259
00:16:56,220 --> 00:16:58,396
Everything went according to my plan.

260
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:03,470
What's that?

261
